    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d620">

                <pb facs="0626" n="620" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg620"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Sir Julian Pauncefote to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-05-14"><hi rendition="#italic">May 14,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to my note of the 1st
                    instant on the subject of affairs in Samoa, I have the honor, in accordance with
                    instructions from the Earl of Kimberley, to inclose copy of dispatch from Her
                    Majesty’s <pb facs="0627" n="621" xml:id="pg621"/> consul at Apia, reporting the
                    steps taken by the consular representatives of the three powers, with a view to
                    the restoration of peace in the Navigators Islands.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Julian
                    Pauncefote.</hi></signed></closer>



